script/"},{"c":"GOLF 2025 Q4","e":"golf","d":"2026-02-26","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"David Maher","x":"We do not take it lightly, but again, so far, so good, and again, first half of 2026, you will see some equipment price increases across our lines, really attached to new club products.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/26/acushnet-golf-q4-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"GOLF 2026 Q1","e":"golf","d":"2026-05-06","l":"streaming","r":"management","s":"Sean Sullivan","x":"That's the fitting network, along with, obviously, a lot of technology unlocks as well, whether it be the ERP system or other digital direct-to-consumer activities.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/05/07/acushnet-golf-q1-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"GOLF 2026 Q1","e":"golf","d":"2026-05-06","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"David Maher","x":"FootJoy profitability, while still burdened with incremental tariffs, is on track with our internal plans.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/05/07/acushnet-golf-q1-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"GOLF 2026 Q1","e":"golf","d":"2026-05-06","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Sean Sullivan","x":"Gross profit in the first quarter of $355 million was up $18 million compared to the first quarter of 2025, mainly due to higher net sales, which were partially offset by higher tariff costs of $17 million year-over-year.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/05/07/acushnet-golf-q1-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"GOLF 2026 Q1","e":"golf","d":"2026-05-06","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Matthew Boss","x":"Or any pushback on any recent pricing or price increases across categories that you would call out?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/05/07/acushnet-golf-q1-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"GOLF 2026 Q1","e":"golf","d":"2026-05-06","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Noah Zatzkin","x":"I guess, first, just wondering what you're seeing in terms of year-over-year price increases from competitors and where you think you stack up there as well as any thoughts on the current state of channel inventories?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/05/07/acushnet-golf-q1-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"GOLF 2026 Q1","e":"golf","d":"2026-05-06","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Sean Sullivan","x":"As is our practice at this time of the year, we are maintaining our full year outlook and continue to expect full year 2026 net sales to be in the range of $2,625 million and $2,675 million and adjusted EBITDA to be in the range of $415 million to $435 million.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/05/07/acushnet-golf-q1-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"GOLF 2026 Q2","e":"golf","d":"2026-08-06","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"David Maher","x":"This growth contributed to a 46% increase in adjusted EBITDA, which, while healthy on its own merits, also reflects the net benefit from tariff refunds.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/08/13/acushnet-golf-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"GOLF 2026 Q2","e":"golf","d":"2026-08-06","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Sean Sullivan","x":"These results include IEEPA tariff refunds, which represented an approximately $38 million benefit to adjusted EBITDA, net of the impact on incentive compensation.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/08/13/acushnet-golf-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"GOLF 2026 Q2","e":"golf","d":"2026-08-06","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Sean Sullivan","x":"We are raising our full year outlook to reflect our solid first half results and the onetime benefit from the net IEEPA tariff refunds.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/08/13/acushnet-golf-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"GOLF 2026 Q3","e":"golf","d":"2026-11-04","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"David Maher","x